# =============================================================================
# GENERATED FILE - do not edit by hand.
# The runtime prelude embedded in every emitted program, expressed as PatLang
# source, split into named chunks mirroring rust-runtime/src/ir/codegen.rs's
# ChunkId split (Stage 37A: host-function prelude chunking). Regenerate after
# changing the host codegen template's chunk constants.
# emit_chunk_<name>() reproduces RustCodegen::<CHUNK> byte-for-byte per chunk
# (parity-checked against codegen_prelude_chunk(name) by the test suite).
# emit_runtime_rs_for(names) concatenates the named chunks in the same fixed
# canonical order the Rust side uses in ChunkId::CANONICAL_ORDER, plus the
# dynamically-assembled call_dispatch glue -- order must match exactly or
# byte-for-byte parity breaks on ordering alone, independent of content.
# emit_runtime_rs() is emit_runtime_rs_for(<all chunks>), kept for backward
# compatibility with existing tooling that calls the whole-prelude form.
# =============================================================================

